  "body": "Extend [PR #985](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/985) from constant site coefficients to the nonconstant quadratic\ndiagonal `D_j=exp(2 pi i a j^2/m)`. The leaf adds an approximation to\n`(I-b D Z^w D^-1)^-1 x` to an arbitrary dirty target and restores the source\nexactly. Its negative call reverses the complete grid word. The complete\nfactor interface keeps the original logarithmic borrowed-array count,\nrestores every borrowed array, and pays four phase passes around the whole\nword. No phase array, cache, or free phase lookup is used.\n\nReview files: [Proof and scope](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/blob/99c71d385171480ecc2c43287aa4a04e1027fcd9/research/dirty-stride-phases/PROOF.md) \u00b7 [Evidence](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/blob/99c71d385171480ecc2c43287aa4a04e1027fcd9/research/dirty-stride-phases/VALIDATION.json) \u00b7 [Source pins and credit](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/blob/99c71d385171480ecc2c43287aa4a04e1027fcd9/research/dirty-stride-phases/SOURCE.json).\n\nThe family includes the retained single-axis periodic chirp\n`exp(-pi i s j^2/t)` for even `L=t`. For `L=8,a=-3,m=16,w=3`, the edge phases\nhave residues `11,9,7,5,3,1,15,13`; the ideal response differs from the\nunphased response by more than `1/8` in a real component.\n\nThe implementation uses exact finite differences, a rounded Machin/Taylor\nevaluator, three reversible real shears, and exact quarter-turns. The proof\nbounds coefficient error and both directions of rounded conjugation,\nincluding large dirty targets. Phase preparation costs `O((L+1)P)` scalar\nsteps with `P=W+O(log W)`. The full bill includes descriptors, input and\nscratch storage, scalar widths, recurrence counters, data access, and tape\nreturns. This is a slower paid phase interface, with no fast-bit or runtime\nspeedup claim.\n\nReproduce with Python 3.11 or later and the standard library:\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -O -B research/dirty-stride-phases/verify.py\npython3 -I -O -B research/dirty-stride-phases/test_package.py\n```\n\nThe primary receipt checks 910 phase cases, 263 rounded leaves, 20 complete\nfactor words, two retained radix-four polynomial kernels, four larger tape\nfixtures, and eight invalid-input controls. The kernel checks pay the exact\nfactor residual and execution error to a 128-bit total budget. All leaf\nnumerical cases have nonzero error; dirty data reaches `2^80`. Separate\nfull-angle rational intervals, geometric sums, and dense Gaussian elimination\nsupply the numerical oracles.\n\nThe package harness rejects 12 semantic, source, and type faults, then\nregenerates the same receipt from a read-only relocated copy. Literal array\naccesses are checked independently of the meter. Phase-shear intermediates\nare measured; Machin integer widths use the stated analytical bound. Receipt\nSHA256: `3305f81e9befe11133e85e0e38b5f0824c7a520d02e1799d5bf703e0bd1df740`.\n\nLocal isolated optimized checks pass on macOS arm64 / Python 3.14.7, as do\nselected-record integrity and all 25 selected-result tests. The primary\nreplay took 65.20 seconds and the complete package harness 63.62 seconds;\nthese are verification durations. The scoped Python 3.11/3.14 workflow is\nincluded; hosted CI and local Python 3.11 execution are separate. The full\nrepository suite and selected cold replay were not run for this isolated\naddition. [VALIDATION.json](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/blob/99c71d385171480ecc2c43287aa4a04e1027fcd9/research/dirty-stride-phases/VALIDATION.json) records the exact source freeze and limits.\n\nBase: [8bddbee377e2f3ce1f1247196c4b290d55767d20](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/commit/8bddbee377e2f3ce1f1247196c4b290d55767d20). [PR #985](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/985) remains pinned at\n[9df42a99dd8497b6e7d46cd2507bb89071372640](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/commit/9df42a99dd8497b6e7d46cd2507bb89071372640), and [PR #479](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/479) at\n`40dd01058439cdffae3e3b41c4fe52edaccf5f91`. The local derived solver has two\nread-once validation edits because the pinned expressions each read twice\nbut charge once. The complete [DERIVATION.diff](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/blob/99c71d385171480ecc2c43287aa4a04e1027fcd9/research/dirty-stride-phases/DERIVATION.diff) is retained beside the\nbyte-exact original. No inverse arithmetic or transport instruction changes.\nAll 14 retained source files have SHA256 and Git-blob pins.\n\nCredit Ali Romman (@aliromman)'s [PR #985](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/985), Rohan Guliani (@Rohansguliani)'s [PR #846](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/846), Charles Bethin (@cbethin)'s [PR #764](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/764),\nChafik Boukhalfa (@chafreaky)'s [PR #479](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/479) and [PR #628](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/628), Ross Richardson (@RossRichardson)'s [PR #948](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/948) for related\nindependent phase-state verification, and the retained manuscript lineage.\nNew material is prepared for Ali Romman (@aliromman), with substantial\nOpenAI Codex assistance; original licenses and notices are retained.\n\nNo new kappa is claimed. The selected frontier and [upstream/](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/tree/99c71d385171480ecc2c43287aa4a04e1027fcd9/upstream) are unchanged.\nThis does not implement the multi-axis stream, arbitrary supplied phase\narrays, variable magnitudes, full transform, constant-coefficient precision\nimprovement, scalar bit-reversible compiler, physical supplier hosting, or\nmultiplication reduction. The finite checks support the written proof and\nare not formal verification or independent human peer review.\n\nCoordinator review: the proof, implementation and complete cost were read. A separate optimized package replay passed all 12 controls and reproduced the receipt from a read-only relocated copy.\n",
